WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:04.420
Hello.

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:10.960
I'm a professor of psychiatry at Seoul
National University Bundang Hospital.

3
00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:15.480
In this fourth session, we will
look at why mood disorders happen,

4
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:19.180
and how temperament and personality are related.

5
00:00:20.150 --> 00:00:23.390
A mood disorder is a biological illness.

6
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:31.170
Apart from environmental factors, constitutional
factors account for fifty to sixty percent.

7
00:00:31.390 --> 00:00:36.150
It means this is not an illness
you can control just by willpower.

8
00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:39.670
It is an illness in which brain function changes.

9
00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:44.990
Our brain has a mood regulation
circuit that regulates mood.

10
00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:49.130
This circuit lets you feel the
mood that fits the situation,

11
00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:52.630
and keeps that mood to an appropriate degree.

12
00:00:52.850 --> 00:00:55.070
But when this circuit becomes loose,

13
00:00:55.090 --> 00:01:01.000
mood goes beyond the normal range and
becomes too elevated or too depressed.

14
00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:08.930
In the brain, several neurotransmitters
stay in balance and regulate mood, energy,

15
00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:10.560
and motivation.

16
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:18.600
When nerve cell activity or neurotransmitters
increase or decrease too much and the balance breaks,

17
00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:23.970
mood and energy become imbalanced,
and a mood disorder appears.

18
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:29.630
The immune system and the brain's neurotransmission
proteins are also known to be involved.

19
00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:33.140
Some factors affect nerve cell activity.

20
00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:35.280
The first is hormones.

21
00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:40.420
Mood disorders easily appear
for the first time, or relapse,

22
00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:47.680
during times of big hormonal change: puberty,
pregnancy and after childbirth, and menopause.

23
00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:49.820
Next is sunlight.

24
00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:57.200
Sunlight affects the production of melatonin,
which regulates sleep, and serotonin,

25
00:01:57.220 --> 00:01:59.100
which regulates mood.

26
00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.040
Relapses are more frequent in
early spring and late autumn,

27
00:02:03.060 --> 00:02:07.440
which is related to sudden
changes in the amount of sunlight.

28
00:02:07.660 --> 00:02:14.120
Less sunlight can make you feel down, but
getting plenty of sunlight, or light therapy,

29
00:02:14.140 --> 00:02:19.610
which uses light as treatment,
can improve mood and motivation.

30
00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:27.140
A strong sense of pride or a perfectionistic
personality, stress in relationships,

31
00:02:27.160 --> 00:02:31.860
sudden shocks like resigning from
a job, bereavement, or bankruptcy,

32
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.570
and long-lasting stress can also

33
00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:39.610
affect whether a mood disorder develops or relapses.

34
00:02:39.830 --> 00:02:40.490
However,

35
00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:47.640
these factors trigger the illness when a temperament
prone to mood disorders is already there.

36
00:02:48.610 --> 00:02:52.430
Temperament is the overall
emotional character a person has.

37
00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:59.550
It consistently affects thoughts, emotions,
behavior, and relationships with other people.

38
00:03:00.630 --> 00:03:02.375
Innate temperament usually lasts for life,
but it is also shaped by the environment,

39
00:03:02.395 --> 00:03:08.690
such as how a person was raised.

40
00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:13.070
People with certain temperaments have
a higher risk of mood disorders,

41
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:18.830
and even with the same mood disorder, the
symptoms differ depending on temperament.

42
00:03:19.050 --> 00:03:24.350
Also, some people live thinking it
is only a matter of temperament,

43
00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:29.330
and after an examination it
turns out to be a mood disorder.

44
00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:37.000
People with a temperament in which mood is hard to
regulate are sensitive to rejection and criticism,

45
00:03:37.020 --> 00:03:40.300
and depend heavily on others emotionally.

46
00:03:40.520 --> 00:03:45.440
They are strongly jealous, and
strongly eager to please other people.

47
00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:48.440
Sometimes they feel full of confidence,

48
00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:53.920
and at other times feel like
a person of no worth at all.

49
00:03:53.940 --> 00:03:58.180
Impulsive binge drinking or binge eating may repeat.

50
00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:05.650
Symptoms of a mood disorder can harden into
something like personality over a long time.

51
00:04:05.670 --> 00:04:11.740
This is especially so when a person has
had a mood disorder since childhood.

52
00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:15.540
For example, you approach people easily when elevated,

53
00:04:15.560 --> 00:04:19.960
but experiences of becoming depressed
over small rejections build up,

54
00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:24.640
and you become sensitive in relationships
and find it hard to trust people.

55
00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:31.480
In this way, mood symptoms create experiences
and environments, these become personality,

56
00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:35.940
and that personality can in
turn worsen the mood disorder.

57
00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.220
So even when medication improves mood symptoms,

58
00:04:39.240 --> 00:04:43.380
a personality built up over many
years may not change easily.

59
00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:47.780
It takes time, and counseling therapy alongside helps.

60
00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:56.690
The Mood Disorder Clinic at Seoul National University
Bundang Hospital is doing research on genetics,

61
00:04:56.710 --> 00:04:58.990
brain waves, and brain imaging.

62
00:04:59.010 --> 00:05:03.420
If you would like to take part,
please talk with your doctor.

63
00:05:03.640 --> 00:05:08.280
Next time, we will look at the
treatment and recovery process,

64
00:05:08.300 --> 00:05:10.840
and why maintenance treatment matters.

65
00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.000
Thank you.
